---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="New Construction Painting in Poinciana | Punch-List & Touch-Ups"
  description="Painting for new construction homes in Poinciana, FL. Builder punch-list repairs, drywall touch-ups, and post-construction painting."
  ogImage="/images/interior-painting.jpg"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/poinciana-new-construction-painting/#article",
        "headline": "New Construction Painting in Poinciana",
        "description": "Post-construction painting, builder punch-list repairs, and drywall touch-ups for new homes in Poinciana, FL.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/poinciana-new-construction-painting/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Poinciana New Construction Painting",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/poinciana-new-construction-painting"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Poinciana New Construction Painting</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">New Construction Painting in Poinciana</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        Post-construction painting, builder punch-list repairs, and drywall touch-ups for new Poinciana homes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            <a href="/areas/poinciana" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Poinciana</a> has seen steady new home construction over the past decade. If you've bought a new construction home, you've likely noticed imperfections—drywall touch-ups needed, uneven paint coverage, scuffs from move-in, or spots the builder missed. Here's how to handle post-construction <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting-poinciana" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">painting</a> and punch-list repairs.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Common Builder Paint Issues</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            New construction paint is done fast. Builders use crews who paint dozens of homes under tight deadlines. Quality varies. Common issues we see in new Poinciana homes:
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Thin Coverage & Streaky Walls</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Builder-grade paint is often sprayed in a single coat over primer. Light colors (white, beige, gray) look fine at first but show primer underneath in certain light. Walls look uneven, streaky, or patchy.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Fix:</strong> Roll a second coat of quality paint (Benjamin Moore Regal Select or Sherwin-Williams Duration). Cost: $1.50-$2.50/sq ft for a full-coverage second coat.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Drywall Imperfections</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Nail pops, visible seams, unfilled screw holes, rough patches. These show up after the home settles or when sunlight hits walls at an angle.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Fix:</strong> Fill holes with <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">drywall compound</a>, sand smooth, prime, touch up paint. Cost: $150-$400 depending on how many spots need fixing.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Sloppy Trim & Cut Lines</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Paint overspray on <a href="/services/trim-crown-molding" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">trim</a>, uneven edges where walls meet ceilings, gaps in caulk, baseboards not caulked to walls.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Fix:</strong> Re-tape and cut clean lines, caulk gaps, repaint trim. Proper trim painting costs $1-$3/linear foot.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Scuffs & Damage from Move-In</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Moving furniture, appliance delivery, and foot traffic before paint fully cured leave scuffs, scratches, and dings. New paint needs 2-4 weeks to fully harden in Florida humidity.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Fix:</strong> Touch up scuffs with matching paint. Keep leftover paint from builder for touch-ups, or we can color-match.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Builder paint quality:</strong> Most builders use single-coat sprayed paint to save time and cost. It meets code and looks okay at closing, but doesn't hold up as well as two coats of quality paint. Upgrading paint during construction (if offered) or repainting after move-in improves durability.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Builder Warranty & Punch-List Process</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">What's Covered</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Most Florida new home builders offer a 1-year warranty covering workmanship defects, including paint and drywall. Covered items typically include:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Drywall cracks or nail pops that appear within the first year</li>
            <li>Peeling or bubbling paint</li>
            <li>Visible seams or unfinished areas</li>
            <li>Unpainted trim or missed spots</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">What's Not Covered</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Normal wear and scuffs after move-in</li>
            <li>Paint quality (thin coverage is not a defect if it meets minimum standards)</li>
            <li>Color dissatisfaction (builder chooses standard colors)</li>
            <li>Cosmetic issues that don't affect function</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Punch-List Timeline</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Most builders schedule a punch-list walk-through at closing or within 30 days. You document issues, builder sends crews to fix them. Timeline:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Day 0-30:</strong> Punch-list walk-through with builder rep. Take photos, list all paint/drywall issues.</li>
            <li><strong>Day 30-90:</strong> Builder schedules repairs. Paint touch-ups typically happen 60-90 days post-closing.</li>
            <li><strong>After 90 days:</strong> If issues persist or new ones appear (settling cracks), submit warranty claims before 1-year mark.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">When to Hire Your Own Painter</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Builder warranty covers defects, not upgrades or cosmetic improvements. Hire your own painter if you want:
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Better Paint Quality</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Builder paint is thin. A second coat of premium paint (Benjamin Moore, Sherwin-Williams) gives richer color, better coverage, and lasts longer. Most new Poinciana homeowners repaint accent walls or entire homes within 1-2 years for better quality.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Custom Colors</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Builders use neutral beiges and grays. If you want bold accent walls, custom colors, or different colors per room, you'll need to repaint after closing. See our <a href="/guides/how-much-does-painting-cost-kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">painting cost guide</a>.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Murals or Specialty Finishes</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <a href="/services/murals-poinciana" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kids room murals</a>, accent walls with texture, or decorative finishes. Builders don't offer these—hire a painter after move-in.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Faster Turnaround</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Builder warranty repairs can take 60-90 days to schedule. If you want touch-ups done immediately after move-in, hiring your own painter is faster.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Post-Construction Painting Cost</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Cost depends on scope. Typical new construction painting projects in Poinciana:
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Touch-Ups & Drywall Repairs</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Minor touch-ups (5-10 spots):</strong> $150-$300</li>
            <li><strong>Moderate repairs (drywall patches, caulking, repaint sections):</strong> $300-$600</li>
            <li><strong>Full room touch-up & second coat:</strong> $400-$800 per room</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Full Repaint (Better Coverage)</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Single room (bedroom, office):</strong> $400-$700</li>
            <li><strong>Living room or master bedroom:</strong> $600-$1,200</li>
            <li><strong>Whole house interior (2,000 sq ft):</strong> $3,500-$6,500</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Prices include prep, two coats of quality paint, and trim touch-ups.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Choosing Paint for New Homes</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            If repainting after builder work, use quality paint that holds up in Florida:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Walls:</strong> Benjamin Moore Regal Select (eggshell or satin) or Sherwin-Williams Duration (matte or eggshell)</li>
            <li><strong>Trim & doors:</strong> Semi-gloss for durability and easy cleaning</li>
            <li><strong>Ceilings:</strong> Flat white ceiling paint</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Quality paint costs $40-$70/gallon but lasts 7-10 years vs. 3-5 years for builder-grade paint.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Best Practices for New Poinciana Homeowners</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Document everything at closing:</strong> Walk through with a flashlight and take photos of paint issues before furniture arrives</li>
            <li><strong>Wait 30-60 days before painting:</strong> Let the house settle. Drywall cracks often appear in the first month.</li>
            <li><strong>Keep leftover builder paint:</strong> Ask builder for extra paint cans for touch-ups. Label them by room.</li>
            <li><strong>Submit warranty claims early:</strong> Don't wait until month 11 to report issues—give builder time to fix before warranty expires</li>
            <li><strong>Upgrade paint before move-in if possible:</strong> Some builders let you upgrade to premium paint packages—worth it if offered</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Common New Construction Paint Questions</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Should I repaint my new home?</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Not always necessary. If builder paint looks good and covers well, touch up scuffs and live with it. If walls look streaky or you want custom colors, repainting main living areas is worth it.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Can I paint before the 1-year warranty ends?</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Yes, but document drywall cracks and paint defects before you repaint, or builder may deny warranty claims ("You painted over it, we can't verify the defect").
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">How long should I wait to paint after move-in?</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Wait 30-60 days for the house to settle. New homes develop hairline cracks as framing adjusts to Florida heat and humidity. Patch these before repainting.
          </p>

          <div class="text-center mt-12">
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-6 font-sans">Need painting or touch-ups for your new Poinciana home?</p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="New Construction Painting in Poinciana"
    description="Post-construction touch-ups, drywall repairs, and quality repaints. Serving Poinciana homeowners."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
